      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Importance",
          "content": "Premenstrual syndrome (PMS) is characterized by physical and psychological symptoms in the luteal phase. Leptin can influence PMS as it acts on the hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal axis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Objective",
          "content": "The aim of this study was to evaluate data in the literature about the profile of plasma leptin in women with PMS."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Evidence Acquisition",
          "content": "We performed a search of databases using both descriptors. Three studies were identified. They included 181 participants. Two of these studies found higher leptin levels in women with PMS."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Results",
          "content": "Conflicting results were found regarding the leptin levels in the luteal phase and the correlation between leptin, estradiol, and progesterone levels."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Conclusions and Relevance",
          "content": "Leptin could have a role in the pathophysiology of PMS and indicate degree of severity of PMS. Future studies on the role of leptin in PMS are needed."
        }
      ]},
